% min x subject to x >= 1: the optimum is 1. d1 proves OBJ >= 1, and d2 then states a
% weaker bound, so the proving row is not the last. The VIPR specification asks for the
% last row to prove the claim; exact SCIP writes such trailing rows, and viprcheck accepts
% with a warning that names d1.
VER 1.0
VAR 1 x
INT 0
OBJ min 1 0 1
CON 1 0
c1 G 1 1 0 1
RTP range 1 1
SOL 1
s1 1 0 1
DER 2
d1 G 1 OBJ { lin 1 0 1 } -1
d2 G 0 OBJ { lin 1 0 1 } -1
